                "prose"
              ]
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "Paragraph",
                "set_style": {
                  "style_names": [
                    "lead",
                    "reveal"
                  ]
                },
                "set_text": {
                  "text": "I was born in San Diego and grew up across the region \u2014 the binational corridor that\u2019s been my family\u2019s home for three generations. San Diego\u2013Tijuana"
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "Paragraph",
                "set_style": {
                  "style_names": [
                    "reveal"
                  ]
                },
                "set_text": {
                  "text": "My mother, my uncles, and my abuelos have been operating in real estate on for more than two decades: acquiring parcels, developing them, leasing them, selling them, doing it again. That\u2019s how I learned this business \u2014 on the ground, on both sides of the border, long before any classroom. both sides of the border"
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "Paragraph",
                "set_style": {
                  "style_names": [
                    "reveal"
                  ]
                },
                "set_text": {
                  "text": "By , I was working land transactions alongside my mother. By , I was on construction sites with my uncles \u2014 planning, financing, building, and leasing the apartments and commercial spaces our family developed. By , I had helped take somewhere between thirty and sixty units from raw land to producing income. 16 18 21"
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "Paragraph",
                "set_style": {
                  "style_names": [
                    "reveal"
                  ]
                },
                "set_text": {
                  "text": "Acquisition. Construction. Leasing. Sale. Repeat. The full arc of a real estate venture, run more times than most agents see in their entire careers."
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "Paragraph",
                "set_style": {
                  "style_names": [
                    "reveal"
                  ]
                },
                "set_text": {
                  "text": "On top of that foundation, I built the institutional toolkit. \u2014 a project-based program tied to actual properties, actual investors, and the financial models lenders and acquisition committees actually use. Five years in corporate sales at AT&T and Wyyerd Fiber sharpened the negotiation muscle and funded the transition. A B.S. in Real Estate & Development from UC San Diego DRE-licensed Multifamily Investment & Development Advisor (#02282434)."
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "Paragraph",
                "set_style": {
                  "style_names": [
                    "reveal"
                  ]
                },
                "set_text": {
                  "text": "What that means for you:"
                },
                "set_attributes": {
                  "attributes": [
                    {
                      "name": "data-inline-style",
                      "value": "font-weight:500;color:var(--terra);"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "Paragraph",
                "set_style": {
                  "style_names": [
                    "reveal"
                  ]
                },
                "set_text": {
                  "text": "I\u2019m not a transactional agent. Most agents in San Diego show properties, write offers, and close deals \u2014 I do those things, but my actual value is upstream. on every property worth considering. under SB 9, ADU law, the State Density Bonus, and SB 1123. for partner deals. end to end \u2014 from feasibility through certificate of occupancy and the cash-out refinance after. I run full proformas I model development upside I structure JV waterfalls I project-manage small infill developments"
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "Paragraph",
                "set_style": {
                  "style_names": [
                    "reveal"
                  ]
                },
                "set_text": {
                  "text": "I work as both a real estate professional a developer. Most people in this business pick one lane \u2014 the lanes inform each other. My development experience changes how I underwrite acquisitions, and my acquisition discipline changes how I run development projects. and"
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "Paragraph",
                "set_style": {
                  "style_names": [
                    "reveal"
                  ]
                },
                "set_text": {
                  "text": "If you\u2019re buying your first multifamily, scaling a portfolio, or looking at what\u2019s buildable on the lot you already own \u2014 I bring real estate finance, development experience, and deep knowledge of the to the table. San Diego\u2013Tijuana region Not just a transaction."
                }
              }
            ]
          },
